34	/**
35	 * Programmatic "(location) (service)" marketing landing pages, the region-tier
36	 * umbrella pages above them, AND (added here) the game-family × location
37	 * matrix + the general per-location VPS/Game-Server pages that don't already
38	 * exist via the tables above — see lib/marketing/gameLocationLandings.ts's
39	 * file doc for the full architecture note.
40	 *
41	 * Four data tables, one route: a slug is checked against the region matrix,
42	 * then the city matrix, then the game×location matrix, then the general
43	 * new-location matrix — in that order, so nothing here can ever shadow a
44	 * hand-written static marketing page (which wins at request time anyway) or
45	 * silently collide with an existing slug. Anything in none of the four falls
46	 * through to a 404. Real DB rows (VPS `Plan` or, for a game×location combo,
47	 * that family's real `GamePlan` rows) feed every page's pricing grid and
48	 * Product rich-result — nothing here is a hardcoded price.
49	 */
